{"name":"Shaded Fuchsia","hex":"#664348","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"shaded","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Being in the shade, not in direct light.","Having a slight colour added (of a diagram or picture) or being slightly darkened as if in the shade."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of shade"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shaded"},{"term":"fuchsia","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A popular garden plant, of the genus Fuchsia, of the Onagraceae family, shrubs with red, pink or purple flowers.","A purplish-red colour, the color of fuchsin, an aniline dye."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a purplish-red colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fuchsia"}],"entries":[{"title":"Shading","blocks":[{"text":"Shading refers to the depiction of depth perception in 3D models or illustrations by varying the level of darkness. Shading tries to approximate local behavior of light on the object's surface and is not to be confused with techniques of adding shadows, such as shadow mapping or shadow volumes, which fall under global behavior of light."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Flatshading01.png/330px-Flatshading01.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shading"},{"title":"Fuchsia","blocks":[{"text":"Fuchsia is a genus of flowering plants that consists mostly of shrubs or small trees."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Brincos_De_Princesa.jpg/330px-Brincos_De_Princesa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fuchsia"},{"title":"Fuchsia (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Fuchsia is a vivid pinkish–red color, named after the color of the flower of the fuchsia plant, which was named by a French botanist, Charles Plumier, after the 16th-ce